WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:01.590
Welcome back to the David Pakman show.

00:00:01.590 --> 00:00:05.660
I am Karen cousins from marina fires sitting
in for David Packman today.

00:00:05.660 --> 00:00:08.090
Uh, we had a pretty busy Monday.

00:00:08.090 --> 00:00:13.179
Obviously lots of bad news coming out for
Donald Trump and lots of things Donald Trump

00:00:13.179 --> 00:00:17.811
did that he thought were going to make his
life so much easier, but in fact, they're

00:00:17.811 --> 00:00:20.430
really just going to make it a living nightmare.

00:00:20.430 --> 00:00:27.220
And one of those things was that the DOJ ordered
former White House counsel Don McGahn to not

00:00:27.220 --> 00:00:30.640
comply with a congressional subpoena.

00:00:30.640 --> 00:00:34.840
Then Don McGahn, through his attorneys, made
it clear to Congress that he was not going

00:00:34.840 --> 00:00:40.700
to be showing up today Tuesday or the hearing
that they wanted to have.

00:00:40.700 --> 00:00:48.710
He wasn't going to give his testimony because
the DOJ told him not to comply.

00:00:48.710 --> 00:00:53.330
That is called, um, obstruction folks.

00:00:53.330 --> 00:00:54.890
You can't do that.

00:00:54.890 --> 00:00:57.410
You're suborning that.

00:00:57.410 --> 00:01:00.730
That's exactly what just happened with Don
McGahn.

00:01:00.730 --> 00:01:05.980
Democrats obviously want the opportunity to
speak to don McGahn because according to the

00:01:05.980 --> 00:01:12.790
Mueller report, McGann played a central role
in telling Mueller and the investigators about

00:01:12.790 --> 00:01:16.720
potential obstruction of justice on behalf
of the president of the United States.

00:01:16.720 --> 00:01:23.400
This is obstruction that McGann claims Donald
Trump committed or was involved directly in.

00:01:23.400 --> 00:01:27.580
So Democrats rightfully want to know more.

00:01:27.580 --> 00:01:29.480
They need some more answers on this.

00:01:29.480 --> 00:01:35.300
They need to see if there was intent to obstruct
justice because if there was, then they absolutely

00:01:35.300 --> 00:01:41.360
100% could move forward with articles of impeachment
against the president based on obstruction

00:01:41.360 --> 00:01:42.360
of justice.

00:01:42.360 --> 00:01:46.479
Now, don't get me wrong, they're already sitting
on a plethora of information on which they

00:01:46.479 --> 00:01:50.310
could impeach the president, but they want
more.

00:01:50.310 --> 00:01:51.670
They want to make it foolproof.

00:01:51.670 --> 00:01:57.299
They want to hit him with all of the charges
that they possibly could, which is completely

00:01:57.299 --> 00:01:59.000
unnecessary.

00:01:59.000 --> 00:02:02.590
I you look at the poll numbers right now,
a majority of people do think that the Mueller

00:02:02.590 --> 00:02:07.780
report made Trump look worse, made it seem
like he did commit some kind of crime.

00:02:07.780 --> 00:02:10.800
That crime is likely obstruction of justice.

00:02:10.800 --> 00:02:13.780
Don McGahn got subpoenaed.

00:02:13.780 --> 00:02:18.370
He is still also a lawyer with the Jones Day
law firms, so it would be interesting to know

00:02:18.370 --> 00:02:23.990
what Jones Day has to say about one of their
own lawyers disregarding a subpoena thinking

00:02:23.990 --> 00:02:27.150
that they are above the law.

00:02:27.150 --> 00:02:28.530
You can't ignore a subpoena folks.

00:02:28.530 --> 00:02:30.670
I mean, let's get that out of the way right
now.

00:02:30.670 --> 00:02:35.810
If you get subpoenaed, you are legally obligated
to show up and the House of Representatives

00:02:35.810 --> 00:02:40.120
does have a mechanism to force this.

00:02:40.120 --> 00:02:41.690
They subpoenaed McGann.

00:02:41.690 --> 00:02:43.450
He said, I'm not showing up.

00:02:43.450 --> 00:02:48.240
They can send the sergeant at arms to go and
arrest him, throw him in the little bitty

00:02:48.240 --> 00:02:53.900
jail that they have right there at the House
of Representatives until he agrees to testify.

00:02:53.900 --> 00:03:01.440
They have the authority and the power to do
that, but they're not going to, and that's

00:03:01.440 --> 00:03:06.620
the most disappointing thing out of all of
this is that they're not going to do just

00:03:06.620 --> 00:03:11.069
going to set up yet a another legal battle
against the president.

00:03:11.069 --> 00:03:17.310
The Democrats are likely going to win just
like they're winning the other ones, but time's

00:03:17.310 --> 00:03:18.810
a factor, right?

00:03:18.810 --> 00:03:27.420
Or they've got what, 18 months, 18 months
before the election, and if they lose their

00:03:27.420 --> 00:03:34.430
majority in that election, it's not likely,
but it is possible obviously then suddenly

00:03:34.430 --> 00:03:36.480
any talk of impeachment is out the window.

00:03:36.480 --> 00:03:39.750
It will never happen at that point.

00:03:39.750 --> 00:03:46.790
So rather than having to send this to court,
get the courts to enforce it, they'll side

00:03:46.790 --> 00:03:47.790
with the Democrats.

00:03:47.790 --> 00:03:51.900
Then the president appeals and appeals until
he gets all the way to the supreme court.

00:03:51.900 --> 00:03:55.340
That could take more than 18 months.

00:03:55.340 --> 00:03:59.660
And I know based on some of the other cases
that we have already seen, the judges typically

00:03:59.660 --> 00:04:05.480
do expedite these, but we can't guarantee
something like that would happen every single

00:04:05.480 --> 00:04:06.530
time.

00:04:06.530 --> 00:04:12.160
Especially when you have a White House filing
a lawsuit or Democrats filing a lawsuit at

00:04:12.160 --> 00:04:14.319
every possible opportunity.

00:04:14.319 --> 00:04:18.680
Use the mechanisms you have in place, throw
them again in your tiny little jail and wait

00:04:18.680 --> 00:04:25.219
for him to start singing because Mcgann's
made it clear he actually did want to testify,

00:04:25.219 --> 00:04:28.210
but he's kind of between a rock and a hard
place.

00:04:28.210 --> 00:04:34.789
He thinks that it's best to listen to the
president rather than listening to Congress.

00:04:34.789 --> 00:04:38.819
He seems to forget that at the end of the
day, Congress has just as much, if not more

00:04:38.819 --> 00:04:44.589
in this particular situation, power than the
president does and they can make his life

00:04:44.589 --> 00:04:48.370
hell if they choose to do so.

00:04:48.370 --> 00:04:51.969
And I think at this point it's time for them
to choose to do so.

00:04:51.969 --> 00:04:59.039
Not just because of McGann's testimony either,
but to send a message, it's time to tell this

00:04:59.039 --> 00:05:04.749
White House that you are not above the law,
that your administration officials are not

00:05:04.749 --> 00:05:06.330
above the law.

00:05:06.330 --> 00:05:11.560
And that when this branch of the government
that has the responsibility of oversight of

00:05:11.560 --> 00:05:16.400
the executive branch comes calling, you have
to pick up the phone.

00:05:16.400 --> 00:05:19.689
You don't have a choice.

00:05:19.689 --> 00:05:25.449
Unfortunately, leadership in the House of
Representatives right now is at least giving

00:05:25.449 --> 00:05:29.240
the appearance of being exceptionally weak.

00:05:29.240 --> 00:05:36.060
Not saying they are exactly week, but by not
impeaching they're coming across as weak.

00:05:36.060 --> 00:05:39.559
They may have some kind of grand strategy
that we don't know about.

00:05:39.559 --> 00:05:41.249
They may be playing a longer game.

00:05:41.249 --> 00:05:47.360
They may have an ace up their sleeves that
we don't even know exists, but by not knowing

00:05:47.360 --> 00:05:49.650
those things, it makes them look weak.

00:05:49.650 --> 00:05:51.120
It makes them look like they were afraid.

00:05:51.120 --> 00:05:54.909
I mean, we've heard them say that, oh, the
public doesn't support impeachment.

00:05:54.909 --> 00:05:56.590
Who Cares?

00:05:56.590 --> 00:06:01.619
The public didn't support bailing out the
big banks, but you did that anyway.

00:06:01.619 --> 00:06:06.620
The public didn't support the Republican tax
scam, but they did that anyway.

00:06:06.620 --> 00:06:11.280
The public didn't support the Republican's
healthcare plan two years ago, but they tried

00:06:11.280 --> 00:06:17.309
to do that anyway, since when does public
opinion actually weigh on the minds of members

00:06:17.309 --> 00:06:18.779
of Congress?

00:06:18.779 --> 00:06:22.559
You guys every day do stuff that the public
says, that's a bad idea.

00:06:22.559 --> 00:06:24.629
We want this instead.

00:06:24.629 --> 00:06:25.800
You never listened to them.

00:06:25.800 --> 00:06:30.620
And then on this one issue where you shouldn't
listen to them, you're using the public as

00:06:30.620 --> 00:06:34.369
an excuse to not go forward with it.

00:06:34.369 --> 00:06:36.210
Just do it.

00:06:36.210 --> 00:06:39.339
Just do it.

00:06:39.339 --> 00:06:40.710
That's it.

00:06:40.710 --> 00:06:42.840
There's no questioning this.

00:06:42.840 --> 00:06:44.139
There's no being mealy mouth.

00:06:44.139 --> 00:06:46.139
There's no being wishy washy.

00:06:46.139 --> 00:06:52.759
This needs to happen not just to get McGann's
testimony, but to restore some sense of order

00:06:52.759 --> 00:08:20.719
and accountability

00:08:20.719 --> 00:08:23.539
to Congress.

